.IX Title "Lucy::Document::HitDoc 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Document::HitDoc 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Document::HitDoc \- A document read from an index.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 5
\&    while ( my $hit_doc = $hits\->next ) {
\&        print "$hit_doc\->{title}\en";
\&        print $hit_doc\->get_score . "\en";
\&        ...
\&    }
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
HitDoc is the search-time relative of the index-time class Doc; it is
augmented by a numeric score attribute that Doc doesn’t have.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS set_score
.IX Subsection "set_score"
.Vb 1
\&    $hit_doc\->set_score($score);
.Ve
.PP
Set score attribute.
.SS get_score
.IX Subsection "get_score"
.Vb 1
\&    my $float = $hit_doc\->get_score();
.Ve
.PP
Get score attribute.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Document::HitDoc isa Lucy::Document::Doc isa Clownfish::Obj.
